  "question": {
    "text": "The integrating factor of the differential equation $\\left(x^2-1 \\frac{d y}{d x}+2\\right) x y=x$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7UxcG",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{x^2-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gsh4q",
      "text": "\n$x^2-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEXxa",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x^2-1}{x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MBoRD",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{x^2-1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given differential equation is\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left(x^2-1\\right) \\frac{d y}{d x}+2 x y=x \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{d y}{d x}+\\frac{2 x}{x^2-1} \\cdot y=\\frac{x}{x^2-1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThis is in linear form.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Integrating factor }=\\int \\frac{2 x}{x^2-1} d x=\\int_e \\frac{d t}{t} \\\\\n& \\text { where } \\begin{aligned}\n& =x^2-1 \\\\\n& =e^{\\log t}=x^2-1\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nHence, required integrating factor $=x^2-1$.",
    "image": null
  },
